# Line-ending normalization (ADR "Repo-wide line-ending normalization"). Git stores every text file with LF and
# checks it out with LF on every platform, so the `.editorconfig` `end_of_line = lf` + the CI `dotnet format`
# whitespace gate (ADR 0439) can never be fought by a CRLF checkout. `text=auto` auto-detects binary files and
# leaves them byte-for-byte untouched; the explicit `binary` markers below are belt-and-suspenders for the asset
# types we ship so a line-ending conversion can never corrupt them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
# vCard and iCalendar fixtures are WIRE FORMAT, not source: both RFCs specify CRLF, and the repo-wide LF
# normalisation above would otherwise rewrite the seeded demo cards into something a strict parser rejects —
# silently, since our own lenient reader accepts either and every test would still pass (#648).
*.vcf   binary
*.ics   binary
*.png   binary
*.icns  binary
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.snk   binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary

# The ADR index is append-only, and every ADR PR appends to the SAME line region — so two ADR PRs in flight always
# conflict on it, mechanically and pointlessly (three times on 2026-08-17 alone), each conflict forcing a fresh CI
# cycle on the trailing PR. `merge=union` resolves that by keeping BOTH sides' lines instead of raising a conflict,
# which is exactly right for a table nobody edits in place. The index is CURATED, not generated — 96 of its status
# cells and 16 of its titles are deliberately terser or more current than the ADR files they point at, and for
# ADR 0406 the index is the only record that 0503 superseded it — so generating it from the files was rejected: it
# would delete that. Union keeps every cell as written. Its one artifact is ordering (an auto-merged row can land
# out of numeric sequence) and its one risk is a same-line edit being duplicated rather than flagged; both are
# caught by AdrIndexTests, which asserts the table stays sorted, unique, and 1:1 with the files on disk.
docs/adr/README.md merge=union
